An opt-in `--translation-workers N` option of `dafny verify` translates to Boogie, and prepares for verification, up to N of the modules that `--verification-module-window` admits at once, and commits them in the window's order, so generated names, Boogie text, diagnostics, logs and resource counts are the same as with the default N = 1. It requires `--type-system-refresh`, and a translation starts only while the managed heap, plus the mean allocation of a translation for each one in progress, stays below `--verification-module-window-memory`. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/241.
